{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 10,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why standest thou afar off, O LORD? ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "why",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hidest thou ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thyself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in times of trouble?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " pride doth persecute the poor: let them be taken in the devices that they have imagined.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the wicked boasteth of his heart's desire, and blesseth the covetous, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "whom",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD abhorreth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked, through the pride of his countenance, will not seek ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "after God",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not in all his thoughts.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His ways are always grievous; thy judgments ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " far above out of his sight: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as for",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " all his enemies, he puffeth at them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath said in his heart, I shall not be moved: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I shall",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " never ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in adversity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His mouth is full of cursing and deceit and fraud: under his tongue ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mischief and vanity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sitteth in the lurking places of the villages: in the secret places doth he murder the innocent: his eyes are privily set against the poor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He lieth in wait secretly as a lion in his den: he lieth in wait to catch the poor: he doth catch the poor, when he draweth him into his net.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He croucheth, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " humbleth himself, that the poor may fall by his strong ones.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He hath said in his heart, God hath forgotten: he hideth his face; he will never see ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise, O LORD; O God, lift up thy hand: forget not the humble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why doth the wicked contemn God? he hath said in his heart, Thou wilt not require ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast seen ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; for thou beholdest mischief and spite, to requite ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " with thy hand: the poor committeth himself to thee; thou art the helper of the fatherless.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Break thou the arm of the wicked and the evil ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ": seek out his wickedness ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "till",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou shalt find none.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The LORD ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " King for ever and ever: the heathen have perished out of his land.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "LORD, thou hast heard the desire of the humble: thou wilt prepare their heart, thou wilt cause thy ear to hear:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.10.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.10.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To judge the fatherless and the oppressed, that the man of the earth may no more oppress.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
